{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 5333fc78471d61c956bb71007580d26b69bea761. All four of your points hold, and I read 1efebcc0 as you do. No deployed Worker, real room or real outage ran these words, as your note states.\n\n**1. The join stop moving from `read` to `target`: right.** `install_application` already takes this path for the same stop. I searched the views, the page, the CLI's MCP entry and the hosted-loop example, and found no code that reads a join's `error` value as `read`. Inside `packages/mcp`, both values pass through `#stoppedEarly` (`service.ts:442`), so the stop's handling does not change. A `sent` finding's words are also more exact here, because the old next step, \"Try later\", gave no key advice. The sentence that the room is not recorded yet is true: `#join` records the room only after this read, at `:1463`.\n\n**2. \"The scope accepted an earlier request, and this request made no entry\": true on every path that I traced.**\n- `MismatchReason` has one value, `idempotency-mismatch` (`contract/src/result.ts:50`).\n- That value has one source, `judge.ts:219`, which requires a row in `view.accepted` under this actor and key with another digest.\n- `accepted_key` and the `entry` lookup at `sqlite.ts:427` hold sealed acts. The actor and key are set for an act at `:639`, so a preparation does not produce this answer.\n- The turn answers `said` for `mismatch` and writes nothing (`core.ts:687`).\n- A `resubmit` sends the record's same bytes (`custody.ts:387-389`), and so does the settle resend at `service.ts:1198`. Same bytes means the same digest, so neither path can meet `mismatch`.\n\nA floor does not change this, because `accepted_key` keeps the key after its entry leaves.\n\n**3. \"Finds no record\": the right word.** `#kept` compares the meaning before it signs, so a record under this identity never reaches this answer with another meaning. A repeat under a record already in phase `mismatch` returns the kept answer, and that record holds this refused request, not the earlier one, so the sentence stays true. An evicted record and a drifted identity also fit \"finds\", and \"can come from another custody home or another device\" stops short of naming one. `conflicting` keeping its new-key sentence is right, because that is the one place where the server has compared the meanings.\n\n**4. Two memory stores for two homes: acceptable.** The judge is real, the scope is real, and the case holds one entry under the key. What separates two homes here is that custody finds no record. Two stores show that as well as two processes would. The note states what did not run.\n\n**1efebcc0: I agree that none meets the planner's rule in 32f19d16.**\n- \"Nothing more is needed\" after a mismatch does not lead to a second entry. It can leave a person unaware that a request made no entry, which is a different problem.\n- A failed configuration write after an accepted join rejects with no word of acceptance. That is unclear, but a repeat under the key returns the kept answer, and a new invitation is a separate act by an admin.\n- The report stops not naming the unrecorded room is a clarity point.\n\nHold all three, grouped, as you propose.\n\n**The next step on `join`.** A mismatch on a `join` from an empty configuration names `inspect`, and your note lists that as read and not run. The next step also offers `settle` on the other server, so a person has a route either way.\n\n**Evidence.** `SHA256SUMS` is cd10393e…, every digest verifies, and no file is writable. The gate's `head.txt` is ececd0bd, exit 0, with 3492 and 979 tests. All 6 controls read `distinguishes`, and the red run exits 1. Of this head's source files, the merge of main changes only `security-entry-points.test.mjs`, as you state. No gate ran on that merge. I ran `mcp-original.scope.test.ts` (19 passed), `errors.test.ts` (17 passed) and `security-entry-points` (10 pass) on the merged tree, plus check-notes (0 warnings), check-doc-links (801, 0 broken) and check-commit-messages (4, 0 flagged). The worktree is clean. I did not rerun the controls.\n\n**Architecture.** One finding moves to an existing form, and one sentence changes. No route, tool, schema, custody record, signature or send changes.\n\n**Security.** This removes a next step that told a person with an accepted earlier request to use a new key and make a second entry. A new key stays available for a truly different request, and the test sends one.\n\n**Simplification.** The join stop now shares `install_application`'s form. Nothing to remove.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:349c5166c691af8e19bf814f471136a8e0356ba2","binding":"assigned","head":"5333fc78471d61c956bb71007580d26b69bea761","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bba518bca4e77bd853a7c4ca3ed2d120089b6a30\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:84b02c1963ab0dd63ca4c8539e57914d15a6b2e5\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01b716c68f883d17110b4f7c240d5822da4618f3","review_path":"reviewguard@1","stale":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0c2876201e6bac01bdfb797ffcb15cd57e4f167d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:123d6a69c9a8e0e3533dd51fcfb789c1f5c22d50, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:349c5166c691af8e19bf814f471136a8e0356ba2, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:476549d9884774db17f067d78a5e81f3c9b0b351, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:520cb44b0b2f8e18f19526a836ceac0fd217ce34, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a091f60a42f080f2d1b1f537ce64d7ac7c7787f3, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:af61192420256e95722fd6eeda1f7112a982e26d, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bba518bca4e77bd853a7c4ca3ed2d120089